  "job_description": "Java Backend Engineer\nHalden Mutual - Leeds, UK (hybrid)\n\nAbout us\nHalden Mutual insures 900,000 homes and cars across the UK. Our engineering team of 80 is replacing a 20-year-old policy system one service at a time, and we would rather do it carefully than quickly.\n\nThe team\nYou'll join the Claims team, which owns everything from the first notification of loss to the final payout. Our services run on a shared Kubernetes platform looked after by the platform team, and claims handlers work in an internal tool built with Angular. We plan in Jira, but we keep the process light.\n\nResponsibilities\n- Design and build services that replace parts of the legacy claims system.\n- Own the APIs and events shared with the policy and payments teams.\n- Sit with claims handlers to understand their work before changing it.\n- Keep services observable, documented and easy to operate.\n- Help interview and onboard new engineers as the team grows.\n\nWhat we're looking for\n- 5 or more years of Java development.\n- Commercial experience with Spring Boot.\n- Experience designing and running microservices.\n- A habit of writing tests and readable code.\n\nNice to have\n- Event streaming with Kafka.\n- Persistence with Hibernate.\n- Building and shipping images with Docker.\n- Deploying to Kubernetes.\n\nBenefits\n- Hybrid: two days a week in our Leeds office.\n- 28 days of holiday, a 10% pension contribution and discounted home insurance.\n- Paid volunteering days and a well-stocked training budget.\n",
